# What NOT to upload to Vercel on `vercel deploy`.
#
# When this file exists, the Vercel CLI uses it as the authoritative ignore
# list (it does not also apply .gitignore), so two things matter here:
#   1. Secrets MUST be listed — otherwise a normally-gitignored .env.local
#      would be uploaded into the deployment source.
#   2. lib/abis.ts is intentionally NOT listed. It is generated from Foundry
#      artifacts that do not exist on Vercel, so `npm run abis` cannot run in
#      the remote build (vercel.json overrides buildCommand to plain
#      `next build`). The generated file therefore has to ship with the source.

# Secrets — never upload
.env
.env.*

# Dependencies & build output — regenerated on Vercel
node_modules
.next
.vercel

# Local-only tooling, caches, scratch
.shots
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
*.log
.tmp-*
